  "stem": "A shell is fired from a fixed artillery gun with an initial speed of u such that it hits the target on the ground at a distance R from it. If $t_{1}$ and $t_{2}$are the values of time taken by it to hit the target in two possible ways, then the product $t_{1}t_{2}$ is:",
  "options": {
    "A": "$Rg$",
    "B": "$R/g$",
    "C": "$\\frac{R}{2g}$",
    "D": "$\\frac{2R}{g}$"
  },
